('200610','2014','Ed-Dur Archaeological Site','Ed-Dur Archaeological Site','Large ancient trading settlement with a Sun God temple, fortifications, stone buildings and tombs, flourishing around the late 1st century BC to 3rd century AD.','1-2 hours if authorized/open','Morning','Check with UAQ Tourism/Archaeology before going because protected archaeological access may be limited.','Confirm archaeological-site access before visiting','Umm Al Quwain','0','0','','','Protected archaeological site; access conditions vary',4.9,4.8,25.52222,55.62611,'Ed-Dur, Umm Al Quwain','https://culturalmap.gov.ae/en/facilities/ed-dour-archaeological-site',0.55,'2026-10-01 12:00:00',NULL,'attraction',NULL,'budget','na','own','2026-10-01 16:00:00','partial','UAE National Cultural Map and UNESCO Tentative List confirm Ed-Dur as a major Roman-period coastal settlement/trading port with temple, fort and tombs. UNESCO notes the site is fenced/protected. Current walk-in hours were not published, so PARTIAL. [Sources: culturalmap.gov.ae; UNESCO]','2026-10-01'),
